# NOT THE ONE IN EFFECT (#1158).
#
# Every image is built with the repository root as its context (`context: .`
# in release.yml), so Docker reads `/.dockerignore` and never this file. The
# two disagree: this one excludes `configs/`, `docs/`, `*.md` and
# `**/tests/`, and the Dockerfiles `COPY` `configs/` — so if this file ever
# did apply, the build would fail on a missing path rather than quietly
# shipping a smaller image.
#
# Kept, with this note, for anyone who builds with `docker/` as the context by
# hand. Change `/.dockerignore` for anything that must affect CI.

# Build artifacts
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Git
.git/
.gitignore

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Documentation
*.md
docs/

# Flatpak build artifacts
flatpak/.flatpak-builder/
flatpak/build-dir/

# Test files
**/tests/
**/*_test.rs

# Example configs (we want fresh configs in containers)
configs/

# GitHub workflows
.github/
